cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Causality: reading effects from studies you could not randomize"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Roy
    given-names: Abhik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7085-8964"
repository-code: "https://github.com/drabhikroy/causality"
abstract: >-
  An open source R Shiny application for quasi-experimental analysis. Eight
  designs from Shadish, Cook, and Campbell are implemented with their standard
  notation, from one group posttest only through matched comparison,
  difference in differences, interrupted time series, regression discontinuity,
  and instrumental variables. Each result pairs the plain comparison with the
  adjusted estimate and carries an identification check for the assumption its
  design rests on, including a plain refusal to identify an effect where the
  design cannot support one. Estimators are written in base R and dplyr so
  every number traces to readable code, and all computation stays on the local
  machine. An optional language model running on the same machine restates a
  finished result in plainer words without changing any number.
keywords:
  - quasi experimental
  - causal inference
  - propensity score matching
  - difference in differences
  - interrupted time series
  - regression discontinuity
  - instrumental variables
  - R
  - Shiny
  - program evaluation
